%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:dctcp-rst -- the RST of a DCTCP connection carries ECT(0).

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of DcTcp (RFC 8257 section 3.6): "a DCTCP sender ... SHOULD set ECT
on all packets", also on a RST.

The class dctcp-rst: TcpConnection::sendRst() and sendRstAck() put ECT(0) on the RST when the
algorithm needs ECN and the connection uses it. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "dctcp" from the other
algorithms, whose RST is Not-ECT.

Host under test: host1, with DcTcp and classic ECN (tcpEcnMode "rfc3168", a precondition), whose
TcpTestApp connects to host2 at 0.1 s and aborts the
connection at 0.5 s. Observation: level 1, the RST of host1 carries ECT(0) in its IPv4 header.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: dctcp-rst
%# value: "DcTcp"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpRst")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000); })
                 .describe("host1 connects to host2"))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().abort(); })
                 .describe("host1 aborts the connection"))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.rstBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("ipv4.ecn == 2")
             .describe("the RST of host1")
             .within(0.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpRst compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "DcTcp"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host1.tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassDcTcpRst: PASS
